  "course_description": "Selected topics in religious studies. Required for majors.",
  "course_notes": "This senior symposium for Religion majors asks: \"What's the point of a Religion major in 2026?\" It looks to pull together some threads of previous coursework in religious studies as a capstone, but also serves as a steppingstone to look beyond graduation into how the study of religion might contribute to one¿s life. As a capstone to their academic work, students will develop a research paper (15-20 pages) on a topic of their choice. As a steppingstone, students will examine how religious studies might relate to future careers and engagements with diverse communities. Throughout the course, we will invite past Religion majors and people using religious studies in their careers into the classroom. We will also venture out to religious sites in and around Atlanta.",
